{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774472024,"nonce":"16wPKZBwr7swzXTPBJxntLfdQQA=","title":"JAX arrays stored as static PyTree metadata cause JIT recompilation on every model update","message":"## Summary\n\nSeveral feedbax Module constructors store JAX arrays as static (auxiliary) PyTree data. This causes eqx.filter_jit to recompile every time the model is passed as an argument after a parameter update, because the static cache key includes these array values which change with each update.\n\n## Affected locations (confirmed via warnings)\n\n- `feedbax/xabdeef/models.py:82` — Mechanics construction\n- `feedbax/xabdeef/models.py:99` — SimpleStagedNetwork construction\n- `feedbax/bodies.py:177` — Channel construction\n- `feedbax/channel.py:137` — Channel construction\n- `feedbax/bodies.py:190` — efferent Channel\n- `feedbax/bodies.py:200` — FirstOrderFilter construction\n- `rlrmp/intervention_compat.py:56` — intervenor params (rlrmp side)\n\nAll produce: \"A JAX array is being set as static! This can result in unexpected behavior and is usually a mistake to do.\"\n\n## Impact\n\nWhen a feedbax model is passed to eqx.filter_jit as an argument (as in standalone training loops outside TaskTrainer), every parameter update via eqx.apply_updates/eqx.tree_at changes the static arrays in the cache key, forcing recompilation. On TPU, each compilation takes 30+ minutes, making training infeasible.\n\nFeedbax's own TaskTrainer avoids this by pre-flattening the model (`jtu.tree_flatten(model)`) and passing only the flat array list to JIT functions. This workaround is effective but should not be necessary — the underlying Modules should store JAX arrays as dynamic leaves, not static metadata.\n\n## The static arrays\n\nThese appear to be dt values, initial state arrays, mask arrays, and similar constants that are set at construction time and never change. They are stored as aux_data in custom `tree_flatten` implementations or as fields that equinox treats as static (because they're in `__init__` without proper registration as dynamic leaves).\n\n## Proposed fix\n\nFor each affected Module, ensure JAX arrays are stored as proper dynamic PyTree leaves (in `children`, not `aux_data`). These are constant during training — marking them dynamic doesn't mean they'll be updated, it just means JAX won't include their values in the JIT cache key.\n\nThis may require reviewing each Module's `tree_flatten`/`tree_unflatten` or switching from manual PyTree registration to standard eqx.Module field handling (which automatically treats arrays as dynamic).\n\n## Workaround\n\nPre-flatten the model with `jtu.tree_flatten(model)`, pass only the flat array list to JIT functions, and unflatten inside the JIT body. This is what TaskTrainer does and what the rlrmp minimax training script now does.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```python\nimport equinox as eqx\nimport jax\n\nmodel = ...  # any feedbax model from point_mass_nn()\n@eqx.filter_jit\ndef f(model, x):\n    return model(x)\n\n# This recompiles on every call after model update:\nfor i in range(5):\n    f(model, x)  # compiles\n    model = eqx.tree_at(lambda m: m.some_leaf, model, new_value)\n    f(model, x)  # RECOMPILES (should cache hit)\n```\n\nSession: 31fa1977 (rlrmp repo). Bug: d6cc111 (rlrmp repo) for the downstream impact.","files":null}]}